uronal SNAREs transits through hemifusion</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>280</volume><fpage>30538</fpage><lpage>30541</lpage><year>2005</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15980065</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R30"><label>30</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reese</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Heise</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Mayer</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Trans-SNARE pairing can precede a hemifusion intermediate in intracellular membrane fusion</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>436</volume><fpage>410</fpage><lpage>414</lpage><year>2005</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15924133</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R31"><label>31</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wong</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Koppel</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Cowan</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name><name><surname>Wessel</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Membrane hemifusion is a stable intermediate of exocytosis</article-title><source>Dev Cell</source><volume>12</volume><fpage>653</fpage><lpage>659</lpage><year>2007</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17420001</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R32"><label>32</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hofmann</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Self-interaction of a SNARE transmembrane domain promotes the hemifusion-to-fusion transition</article-title><source>J Mol Biol</source><volume>364</volume><fpage>1048</fpage><lpage>1060</lpage><year>2006</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17054985</pub-id></element-citation></ref><r